IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-review`

-- Tests of ei4-part-vi-review.l4 (Act ss 111 to 115). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section,
-- before the module was run; none is copied from the module's output. Dates are chosen so the arithmetic can be done on a calendar:
-- March has 31 days, so 30 days after 1 March is 31 March; 21 days after 1 May is 22 May.

§ `Test requests`

-- A request by a claimant, in the prescribed form, decided on 1 March 2026, made on a day the test chooses.
GIVEN madeon IS A DATE
      further IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `ei4 Request for reconsideration`
`a test request by the claimant made on` madeon `with further time` further MEANS `ei4 Request for reconsideration` WITH
    `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision` IS TRUE
    `the requester is the employer of the claimant` IS FALSE
    `the request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS TRUE
    `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1
    `the day on which the request is made` IS madeon
    `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed` IS further

§ `s 111 -- the Commission may rescind or amend`

-- 111: new facts alone are enough ("if new facts are presented or if it is satisfied ...").
#ASSERT `s 111 the Commission may rescind or amend a decision given in a claim for benefits` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 111: the Commission's satisfaction that the decision was given without knowledge of a material fact is enough on its own.
#ASSERT `s 111 the Commission may rescind or amend a decision given in a claim for benefits` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 111: so is its satisfaction that the decision rested on a mistake as to a material fact.
#ASSERT `s 111 the Commission may rescind or amend a decision given in a claim for benefits` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 111: with none of the three, the section gives no power.
#ASSERT NOT `s 111 the Commission may rescind or amend a decision given in a claim for benefits` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 112(1) -- the thirty days`

-- 112(1)(a): 30 days after the day the decision is communicated (1 March): 31 March, and that day counts (fork F-ei4-1).
#ASSERT `s 112(1)(a) the last day to request a reconsideration within 30 days` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `s 112(1)(a) the request is made within 30 days after the decision is communicated` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `with further time` NOTHING)
-- 112(1)(a): one day later is outside the thirty days.
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(1)(a) the request is made within 30 days after the decision is communicated` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) `with further time` NOTHING)
-- 112(1)(a): the day after the decision is well inside.
#ASSERT `s 112(1)(a) the request is made within 30 days after the decision is communicated` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 2) `with further time` NOTHING)

§ `s 112(1)(b) -- any further time the Commission allows`

-- 112(1)(b): with no further time allowed, the paragraph gives nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(1)(b) the request is made within any further time the Commission has allowed` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) `with further time` NOTHING)
-- 112(1)(b): the Commission allowed until 30 June 2026: 30 June is in time, 1 July is not.
#ASSERT `s 112(1)(b) the request is made within any further time the Commission has allowed` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) `with further time` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(1)(b) the request is made within any further time the Commission has allowed` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) `with further time` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)))

§ `s 112.1 -- decisions not subject to review`

-- 112.1: a decision made under the Regulations about writing off a penalty, an amount payable, or interest, is not subject to review.
#ASSERT `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 112.1: a write-off topic without a decision under the Regulations is not within the section; neither is a decision under the Regulations on another topic.
#ASSERT NOT `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 112.1 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 112(1) and (2) -- a request made under subsection (1), and the duty to reconsider`

-- 112(1): a claimant, in the prescribed form, in time, on a decision that may be reviewed: a request is made under (1).
#ASSERT `s 112(1) a request for reconsideration is made under subsection (1)` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `with further time` NOTHING) FALSE
-- 112(2): then the Commission must reconsider.
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the Commission must reconsider its decision` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `with further time` NOTHING) FALSE
-- 112(1): too late and no further time: no request is made under (1), so no duty to reconsider.
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(1) a request for reconsideration is made under subsection (1)` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) `with further time` NOTHING) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(2) the Commission must reconsider its decision` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) `with further time` NOTHING) FALSE
-- 112(1)(b): too late for the thirty days but within the further time the Commission allowed: the duty arises.
#ASSERT `s 112(2) the Commission must reconsider its decision` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) `with further time` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)))  FALSE
-- 112.1: in time and in form, but the decision is shielded from review: nothing is reconsidered.
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(2) the Commission must reconsider its decision` (`a test request by the claimant made on` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) `with further time` NOTHING) TRUE

§ `s 112(1) -- who may ask, and in what form`

-- 112(1): the employer of the claimant may ask even though it is not the subject of the decision.
#ASSERT `s 112(1) the requester is one of the persons who may request a reconsideration` (`ei4 Request for reconsideration` WITH `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision` IS FALSE, `the requester is the employer of the claimant` IS TRUE, `the request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS TRUE, `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day on which the request is made` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 2, `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed` IS NOTHING)
-- 112(1): a stranger to the decision who is not the claimant's employer may not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(1) the requester is one of the persons who may request a reconsideration` (`ei4 Request for reconsideration` WITH `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision` IS FALSE, `the requester is the employer of the claimant` IS FALSE, `the request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS TRUE, `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day on which the request is made` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 2, `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed` IS NOTHING)
-- 112(1): the request must be in the prescribed form and manner; one that is not is not "made under subsection (1)".
#ASSERT NOT `s 112(1) a request for reconsideration is made under subsection (1)` (`ei4 Request for reconsideration` WITH `the requester is a claimant or other person who is the subject of the decision` IS TRUE, `the requester is the employer of the claimant` IS FALSE, `the request is in the prescribed form and manner` IS FALSE, `the day on which the decision is communicated to the requester` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 1, `the day on which the request is made` IS YearMonthDay 2026 3 2, `the last day of any further time the Commission has allowed` IS NOTHING) FALSE

§ `s 113 -- appeal to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal`

-- 113: a dissatisfied party to a decision made under s 112 may appeal.
#ASSERT `s 113 a party may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 113: "including a decision in relation to further time to make a request": a decision on further time alone is appealable too.
#ASSERT `s 113 a party may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 113: a party who is not dissatisfied has nothing to appeal.
#ASSERT NOT `s 113 a party may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 113: someone who is not a party may not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 113 a party may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 113: a dissatisfied party, but the decision is neither a decision under s 112 nor one about further time: no appeal under this section.
#ASSERT NOT `s 113 a party may appeal the decision to the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 114 -- payment pending appeal`

-- 114(2)(a): the decision was given on 1 May 2026; 21 days after is 22 May. An appeal brought on 22 May on the s 36 ground stops (1).
#ASSERT `s 114(2)(a) the appeal to the Appeal Division stops subsection (1) applying` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 22) TRUE
-- 114(2)(a): brought on 23 May, the 22nd day after, it does not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 114(2)(a) the appeal to the Appeal Division stops subsection (1) applying` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 23) TRUE
-- 114(2)(a): within the 21 days but on some other ground: it does not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 114(2)(a) the appeal to the Appeal Division stops subsection (1) applying` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 10) FALSE
-- 114(2): either limb stops (1): (a) alone.
#ASSERT `s 114(2) subsection (1) does not apply` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 22) TRUE FALSE
-- 114(2)(b): a case prescribed by regulation alone, even where (a) fails.
#ASSERT `s 114(2) subsection (1) does not apply` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) FALSE TRUE
-- 114(2): neither limb.
#ASSERT NOT `s 114(2) subsection (1) does not apply` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) FALSE FALSE
-- 114(1): allowed by the General Division, no exception: payable although an appeal is pending.
#ASSERT `s 114(1) benefits are payable in accordance with the decision even though an appeal is pending` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 114(1): allowed by the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal is just as good.
#ASSERT `s 114(1) benefits are payable in accordance with the decision even though an appeal is pending` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 114(1): not allowed by either, nothing is payable under this subsection.
#ASSERT NOT `s 114(1) benefits are payable in accordance with the decision even though an appeal is pending` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 114(1) with (2): allowed, but an exception in (2) applies: subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `s 114(1) benefits are payable in accordance with the decision even though an appeal is pending` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 114(1): benefits paid after the decision are treated as duly paid and are not recoverable.
#ASSERT `s 114(1) benefits paid after the decision are treated as duly paid and are not recoverable from the claimant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 114(1): benefits paid before the decision are not within the sentence.
#ASSERT NOT `s 114(1) benefits paid after the decision are treated as duly paid and are not recoverable from the claimant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 114(1): where an exception applies there is no such protection (FALSE says only that s 114(1) gives none).
#ASSERT NOT `s 114(1) benefits paid after the decision are treated as duly paid and are not recoverable from the claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 116 to 123 -- repealed`

-- The stub is a string-only definition: it exists so the numbering has no silent gap; it decides nothing.
#EVAL `ss 116 to 123 repealed, and therefore not encoded`
